{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/160548-is-there-anyway-to-combine-promethean-with-wraith","id":160548,"title":"Is there anyway to combine Promethean with Wraith?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-05T21:16:27-07:00","id":160548,"title":"Is there anyway to combine Promethean with Wraith?","content":"Got my hands on Wraith the Oblivion (few of my ventures into cWoD) and a thought struck me. Prometheans suffer on the same level as Wraiths do but are going in two directions in terms of themes (one trying to leave the world while the other is attempting to join it). Is there anyway to shove Wraith into nWoD or am I just going to have to wait for a Giest-Wraith translation guide and importing from that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T21:46:28-07:00","id":160563,"title":"","content":"I think I saw a NWoD conversion of Wriath floating around somewhere at one point. Try Mr.Gone's site. He usually has those things laying around if they exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T22:00:51-07:00","id":160569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/160548-is-there-anyway-to-combine-promethean-with-wraith?p=160563#post160563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I saw a NWoD conversion of Wriath<u><i><b> floating around somewhere at one point</b></i></u>.</div> </div> </div> </div>very punny. Thanks for the tip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T22:13:51-07:00","id":160588,"title":"","content":"There are two Wraith conversions. One is better than the other, but both aren't quite the same.<br /> There's also Mummy: the Curse, which actually has some stealth-errata (in the Numina and Ghosts section) that lets you play fairly functional Wraiths.<br /> Also also, I was working on my own Wraith conversion a while ago, but gave up because if I run Wraith, I'd rather just use it as-is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T23:01:55-07:00","id":160603,"title":"","content":"What Ben said about <b>Mummy</b>. Mind you, that\u2019s pre-GMC (just barely), and the new Ethereal Beings rules don\u2019t always play nice with <b>Mummy</b>\u2019s ghost Numina; but it\u2019s a place to start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T23:43:35-07:00","id":160617,"title":"","content":"Well, what do you want to bring in from Wraith in particular? Just the mirrored themes? Or underlining the reality of souls? Or the twisted Hierarchies of the Damned? Or gaining mortality by stealing it from the dead? Or the degradation of the soul as a cautionary tale for its seekers? The connections that Fetters provide to the living world? Or just the plain fucking awesomeness/awfulness that is/was Wraith: the Oblivion?<br /> <br /> Because they're <i>all </i>good. Even better with Wraith: the Great War.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T00:11:09-07:00","id":160622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/160548-is-there-anyway-to-combine-promethean-with-wraith?p=160617#post160617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, what do you want to bring in from Wraith in particular? Just the mirrored themes? Or underlining the reality of souls? Or the twisted Hierarchies of the Damned? Or gaining mortality by stealing it from the dead? Or the degradation of the soul as a cautionary tale for its seekers? The connections that Fetters provide to the living world? Or just the plain fucking awesomeness/awfulness that is/was Wraith: the Oblivion?<br /> <br /> Because they're <i>all </i>good. Even better with Wraith: the Great War.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mirroring the themes is the main idea and actually seems to be the easiest thing out of all the above. Prometheans come into the world knowing that the world hates them. It actively despises them and their entire existence is geared towards an introverted quest on getting a soul. Wraiths tend to suffer the same thing. They are dumped into the Shadowlands into a world that actively being ripped apart by Oblivion and their only way get out of it is again, an introverted quest on resolving issues that keeps one in that state.<br /> <br /> In a way, I view Prometheans as a reverse Wraith. They come literally from nothing (Oblivion), and either steadily progress towards entry of the world of the living or simply become something.. else. Either way, they are forces of pure creation spawn from the mouth of Oblivion in search of meaning.<br /> <br /> Wraiths on the other hand, try to hold on to meaning long enough to resolve a goal and most don't even know what the goal is. They face an enemy that is ever present and is actively trying to strip away their meaning and experience. The complete opposite of what the goal of a promethean's pilgrimage is about.<br /> <br /> All this combined with the image of a Promethean trek down the Shadow lands with the wasteland not really having any effect because well... the Shadowlands are shit to begin with as Oblivion's maw continues to consume.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T16:22:34-07:00","id":161244,"title":"","content":"What you want are the Lucid Dead and Impassioned Soul Numina from <b>Mummy</b>: the former reformats the ghost to use the traditional nine attributes and skills setup instead of the Ephemeral Beings\u2019 abbreviates \u201cthree attributes\u201d thing; Impassioned Soul modifies the ghost so that it\u2019s now driven by a set of Passions instead of being kept on Earth by Anchors, and puts it on a countdown where it needs to pursue its Passions or face dissolution. Personally, I\u2019ve house-ruled the latter to give Impassioned Souls a Sekhem-like power stat<sup>*</sup> that starts high and degrades over time; the main difference being that when the Impassioned Soul\u2019s power stat runs out, that\u2019s the end for it: if it hasn\u2019t achieved transcendence by then, it\u2019s toast. In the post-GMC WoD, I have this Sekhem-like power stat replace the ghost\u2019s Rank, and I treat the combination of the two Numina plus attendant rules tweaks as the acquisition of a \u201cWraith\u201d greater template by the ghost \u2014 the triggering event occurring when something removes the ghost\u2019s \u201ccaul\u201d, to borrow some terminology from <b>Wraith</b> (i.e., whatever it is that keeps most of nWoD\u2019s ghosts trapped in a half-conscious state, where they\u2019re unable to think lucid thoughts and have their passions subdued).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">* technically more of a hybrid of <b>Mummy</b>\u2019s Sekhem and <b>Geist</b>\u2019s Psyche: I call it Psyche, and impose benefits and drawbacks such as <b>Geist</b>-like Anchors and interaction with the Underworld akin to what Sin-Eaters get. Other stuff I use from <b>Geist</b> are Thresholds (which define favored Numina that are easier to acquire). I\u2019ve considered giving them access to Keys and Manifestations in a manner similar to <b>Geist</b>\u2019s Unfettered Geists (that is, each Key/Manifestation pair as a separate Numina); but that\u2019s still under consideration.</span><br /> <br /> I also give Wraiths a slightly modified Memory stat in place of Morality/Integrity. In short, I run Impassioned Souls very much like Mummies on a Descent, save for them being ephemeral and being on their first, last, and only Descent. Removing a ghost\u2019s caul reignites its passions; but it doesn\u2019t restore its former memories, and those passions are now feeding on the wraith\u2019s very being, putting him in a race against time to remember what his unfinished business is, complete it, and move on to whatever comes next before he burns out.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s much more of a <b>Mummy</b>-like thing than a <b>Promethean</b>-like thing; the main thing I borrow from <b>Promethean</b> is its Milestones and New Dawn mechanics, with \u201cmilestones\u201d being recast as \u201cunfinished business\u201d and \u201cNew Dawn\u201d being recast more along the lines of <b>Wraith</b>\u2019s Transcendence in terms of what happens when it\u2019s successful.<br /> <br /> The biggest differences between this conception of a wraith and oWoD\u2019s wraiths are the lack of a Shadow and Shadowguiding, and the absence of an all-pervasive society of the dead. These wraiths simply don\u2019t stick around long enough to form a cohesive society of their own<sup>\u2020</sup> (instead piggybacking on the societies that ordinary ghosts may or may not have); and the primary conflict is the aforementioned race against the clock instead of an inner struggle against a personal nemesis. If you want to add in the Shadowguiding stuff, go for it; but frankly, these wraiths have enough on their plates without it. But bear in mind that a wraith\u2019s Passions are as capable of driving it to destructive actions as to uplifting ones, especially as they become more desperate; so the \u201cyou are your own worst enemy\u201d thing is still in there \u2014 just not as a separate voice in your head<sup>\u2021</sup>.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">\u2020 Some wraiths died centuries or even millenia ago; but no wraith has been a <i>wraith</i> for more than a decade; and very few survive more than a year or two.<br /> <br /> \u2021 Heck, I\u2019ve even considered the possibility of letting a wraith create a Shade, reminiscent of <b>Changeling</b>\u2019s fetches, onto which the wraith can push its undesirable urges. Not quite a Shadow and Shadowguiding; but close \u2014 and entirely optional: not every wraith has a Shade, and the frequency of this phenomenon is left up to the Storyteller. A possible mechanic for this: tie it to Memory Breaking Points. When you lose a point of Memory due to a degeneration check, you can insulate yourself against further losses by empowering your Shade. If you don\u2019t have one yet, you spawn one immediately; and every time you do this, the Shade picks up an Echo Thematically tied to the Breaking Point you blocked off. Meanwhile, the Shade should have means and motive to interfere in the Wraith\u2019s quest, possibly even a means of destroying and consuming the wraith. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-06-2014, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}